From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0201-builder-survives-bad-alloc.patch

Source: 0201-builder-survives-bad-alloc.patch
Core patch, for tools/eglantine-patches as 0201, after 0200. Ours.

Run 61 (next14, 326 s) ended on thread VkPipelineBuilder with std::bad_alloc. Symbolized with the
next14 symbols the stack is aco::optimize_postRA, aco_compile_shader, radv_shader_nir_to_asm,
radv_graphics_shaders_compile, radv_CreateGraphicsPipelines, GraphicsPipeline::MakePipeline, the
lambda in the GraphicsPipeline constructor, StatefulThreadWorker. ACO is C++ and its operator new
threw: 3420160 bytes is exactly 835 x 4 KiB, pr_opt_ctx's table of one entry per block, with the
heap exhausted. 0181 does not cover this: its catch is in PipelineCache::CreateGraphicsPipeline,
and that frame is not on this stack, because the lambda runs on the worker. The lambda only caught
vk::Exception.

With the switch vk::Device::CreateGraphicsPipeline and CreateComputePipeline turn it into a
vk::Exception for VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY, the error the driver should have returned, and the
catch both lambdas already have ends the build as a failed one: is_built is set, so the GPU
thread's wait ends, and the pipeline stays null. 0200 then drops its draws; a compute pipeline
without a VkPipeline is not dispatched (IsBound). Done in the wrapper so the lambdas stay as they
are: fable-mesh-compute-0181 edits those lines, and its extra compute builds are covered too. The
two driver calls keep their text, because prepare-vulkan-port.py hangs its timers on it. Other
callers (blit helpers, on the GPU thread) get the same vk::Exception, which ends the session there
as the bad_alloc did.

The unwinding goes through RADV's C frames and ACO's (-fno-exceptions, so nothing is cleaned up on
the way). Checked in the next14 symbols: every frame from aco::optimize_postRA to
radv_CreateGraphicsPipelines has an .eh_frame entry. Run 61 itself caught a bad_alloc from this same
new handler at 195 s (144 MiB, decode worker), so throw and catch work on the console, but never
yet across the driver's frames. In RADV's source (f5610fe, the pin in tools/deps.json) no lock is
held across this compile, apart from shader_dump_mtx when dumping. What the driver allocated for
that pipeline (NIR, the ACO program, the radv_pipeline) leaks: for an 835-block shader a few MiB,
maybe tens, at a guess, and each new pipeline of such a shader that fails leaks again. A failed
pipeline is not built again until the cache evicts it.

Switch: EDEN_NX2_PIPELINE_FAIL_SOFT=1. Default off: no handler for bad_alloc is on the stack, so
the exception ends the session as before, with the driver's frames in the crash report (a handler
that rethrew would unwind first and lose them), and 0181's catch still sees an inline build. Not
run. Syntax checked with clang only.

In the log: "No memory for the driver to build a pipeline", then "Graphics pipeline build failed:
VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY ..." (compute: "Adreno rejected compute shader ...").

Memory: nothing new, apart from the leak above. Not a fix for the memory wall: it only turns this
one end into missing draws, and a plain malloc failure in RADV's C code is not covered.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/video_core/vulkan_common/vulkan_wrapper.cpp b/src/video_core/vulkan_common/vulkan_wrapper.cpp
index d0bca88125..2520fff909 100644
--- a/src/video_core/vulkan_common/vulkan_wrapper.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/vulkan_common/vulkan_wrapper.cpp
@@ -5,7 +5,9 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
 
 #include <algorithm>
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <memory>
+#include <new>
 #include <optional>
 #include <utility>
 #include <vector>
@@ -20,6 +22,29 @@ namespace Vulkan::vk {
 
 namespace {
 
+/// EDEN_NX2_PIPELINE_FAIL_SOFT=1 (as PipelineFailSoft in vk_scheduler.h): the driver's shader
+/// compiler (ACO) is C++, and its operator new throws through vkCreate*Pipelines (run 61, on a
+/// builder thread with nobody to catch it). That becomes the error the call should have returned,
+/// so the build ends as a failed one. Unset, no handler is on the stack: the session ends as
+/// before, and the crash report keeps the driver's frames, which a handler that rethrew would lose.
+template <typename Func>
+void DriverPipelineBuild(Func&& build) {
+    static const bool soft = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_PIPELINE_FAIL_SOFT");
+        return value != nullptr && value[0] == '1';
+    }();
+    if (!soft) {
+        build();
+        return;
+    }
+    try {
+        build();
+    } catch (const std::bad_alloc&) {
+        LOG_CRITICAL(Render_Vulkan, "No memory for the driver to build a pipeline");
+        throw Exception(VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY);
+    }
+}
+
 template <typename Func>
 void SortPhysicalDevices(std::vector<VkPhysicalDevice>& devices, const InstanceDispatch& dld,
                          Func&& func) {
@@ -773,20 +798,24 @@ PipelineLayout Device::CreatePipelineLayout(const VkPipelineLayoutCreateInfo& ci
 
 Pipeline Device::CreateGraphicsPipeline(const VkGraphicsPipelineCreateInfo& ci, VkPipelineCache cache) const {
     VkPipeline object = VK_NULL_HANDLE;
-    auto const result = dld->vkCreateGraphicsPipelines(handle, cache, 1, &ci, nullptr, &object);
-    // Adreno 5xx drivers do not properly return when a graphics pipeline fails to be created
-    // Some (unkown) Mali drivers also do not properly return
-    // This result code is out of spec, but should be handled as "kinda working"
-    if (result == VK_INCOMPLETE)
-        return Pipeline(object, handle, *dld);
-    Check(result);
+    DriverPipelineBuild([&] {
+        auto const result = dld->vkCreateGraphicsPipelines(handle, cache, 1, &ci, nullptr, &object);
+        // Adreno 5xx drivers do not properly return when a graphics pipeline fails to be created
+        // Some (unkown) Mali drivers also do not properly return
+        // This result code is out of spec, but should be handled as "kinda working"
+        if (result == VK_INCOMPLETE)
+            return;
+        Check(result);
+    });
     return Pipeline(object, handle, *dld);
 }
 
 Pipeline Device::CreateComputePipeline(const VkComputePipelineCreateInfo& ci,
                                        VkPipelineCache cache) const {
     VkPipeline object;
-    Check(dld->vkCreateComputePipelines(handle, cache, 1, &ci, nullptr, &object));
+    DriverPipelineBuild([&] {
+        Check(dld->vkCreateComputePipelines(handle, cache, 1, &ci, nullptr, &object));
+    });
     return Pipeline(object, handle, *dld);
 }
 
